<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saxon Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">772–804</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> Wars were the campaigns fought from 772 to 804 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> against the Saxons, a Germanic people living east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. The conflict involved repeated annual campaigns, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">mass deportations</a> and the forced Christianisation of the Saxons. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> present the wars as showing both the strengths and limits of Carolingian military power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saxon-wars.jpg" alt="Saxon Wars" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frankish_Empire_481_to_814-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
